  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Node Capabilities**\n\nI\'ve confirmed Node.js version 22.23.3, which includes native type stripping! This is excellent. My next step is to examine the `metadata.json` and `index.html` files, and I\'ve started updating the former, specifying \"JARVIS\" as the name, with the description starting as \"Just A Rather...\"\n\n\n**Defining JARVIS\'s Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining JARVIS\'s core functionalities. I\'ve pinpointed his major capabilities, including server-side Gemini API integration. I\'ve also incorporated necessary permissions like the microphone. I have synced the `index.html` file, including the title and description, as well as the open graph tags.\nI\'m also considering the user experience of JARVIS, to be as authentic as possible. I\'m focusing on the visual design elements.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Interface**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the visual design elements of JARVIS\'s interface. I\'m focusing on the color palette: a dark `#060b13` base with luminous cyan/arc-blue accents (`#00f0ff`, `#0ea5e9`, `#38bdf8`), warning amber/orange (`#f59e0b`, `#ef4444`) for critical alerts, and gold titanium accents (`#eab308`). I\'ve started incorporating futuristic HUD geometry, including corner brackets, grid overlays, and hexagonal matrices, along with interactive Arc Reactor Core visualizers.\n\nI\'ve moved on to the interactive audio system, and am setting up custom synthesized sci-fi sound effects, using the Web Audio API Sound Synthesizer! I am working on the \"JARVIS online\" startup sound (a futuristic chime with ascending harmonics), as well as beep/UI blip sounds, and alert protocol sounds!\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Interaction**\n\nI\'m now integrating voice interaction, including a microphone button and hands-free mode triggered by \"Jarvis...\". The Web Speech API handles automatic transcription, sending commands to the system. For output, I\'ve implemented a real AI voice via `/api/tts` using Gemini, or, as a fallback, browser SpeechSynthesis. An audio visualizer will dynamically oscillate with the audio output!\n\n\n**Defining Operational Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on JARVIS\'s operational capabilities. He\'ll support structured tool actions, and will respond to commands with structured outputs updating the UI. I have considered his HUD mode selector, including Command Center/Terminal mode, Arc Reactor mode, and Stark Armor mode. These modes include interactive UI elements and the ability to diagnose problems, plan operations, or simply converse.\n\n\n**Expanding Operational Protocols**\n\nI\'m now expanding JARVIS\'s operational protocols to encompass detailed diagnostics and tactical capabilities. I\'m focusing on features such as 3D/vector blueprints, integrity percentages, weapon readiness reports, and thruster diagnostics. I\'ve designed a \"Tactical Radar\" and \"Environmental Scan\" for real-time data, and structured protocols, including Clean Slate, House Party, and Veronica Orbital Deployment. I\'m also preparing a \"Diagnostics & Code Terminal\" for live telemetry.\n\n\n"
