  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning Application Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on architecting the JARVIS application. I\'ve begun outlining the essential components and audio tools needed for an impressive interface. Specifically, I\'m considering using `src/utils/soundEffects.ts` with a real-time Web Audio API sound synthesizer, including functions like `playBeep(freq, type, duration)`. My aim is to define the ideal structure.\n\n\n**Defining Audio Framework**\n\nI\'m now refining the audio framework. I\'ve got `playJarvisChime()`, the dual harmonic chime, and `playProtocolAlert()` for warning pulses. Furthermore, I am planning to implement `playScanBlip()`, the sonar blip. I will also add `playReactorCharge()` for a rising oscillator, and `playClick()` for a tactile HUD click. I need to design Mute/Volume controls.\n\n\n**Developing Interface Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating interactive elements into the interface. I\'m focusing on the `HudHeader.tsx` status bar. I\'m adding an Stark Industries emblem, time displays, system status, uplink status, reactor load, and audio toggles. The `CommandCenter.tsx` is under design, including message feeds, voice dictation, quick protocol buttons, and a real-time audio player. I\'m also planning to incorporate sound effects.\n\n\n**Designing Armory & Power Modules**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the armory and power components. I\'m focusing on the `ArmoryModule`, implementing Stark armor schematics, telemetry, and deploy actions with HUD alerts. For the `PowerMatrixModule`, I\'m developing Arc Reactor power routing, distribution sliders, and emergency divert presets. Finally, I\'ll integrate a tactical radar module.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1319933"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * Web Audio API synthesizer for sci-fi JARVIS HUD sound effects.\\n * Synthesizes audio entirely in-browser without external asset dependencies.\\n */\\n\\nclass SoundSynthesizer {\\n  private ctx: AudioContext | null = null;\\n  public isMuted: boolean = false;\\n\\n  private initContext(): AudioContext | null {\\n    if (this.isMuted) return null;\\n    try {\\n      if (!this.ctx || this.ctx.state === \'closed\') {\\n        const AudioCtx = window.AudioContext || (window as any).webkitAudioContext;\\n        if (AudioCtx) {\\n          this.ctx = new AudioCtx();\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if (this.ctx && this.ctx.state === \'suspended\') {\\n        this.ctx.resume();\\n      }\\n      return this.ctx;\\n    } catch {\\n      return null;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Subtle futuristic tactile UI click\\n   */\\n  public playClick(): void {\\n    if (this.isMuted) return;\\n    const ctx = this.initContext();\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const osc = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      const gain = ctx.createGain();\\n\\n      osc.type = \'sine\';\\n      osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(1200, ctx.currentTime);\\n      osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(400, ctx.currentTime + 0.04);\\n\\n      gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.08, ctx.currentTime);\\n      gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, ctx.currentTime + 0.04);\\n\\n      osc.connect(gain);\\n      gain.connect(ctx.destination);\\n\\n      osc.start();\\n      osc.stop(ctx.currentTime + 0.045);\\n    } catch {\\n      // Audio playback failsafe\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * High-tech electronic sonar / telemetry scan blip\\n   */\\n  public playScanBlip(): void {\\n    if (this.isMuted) return;\\n    const ctx = this.initContext();\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const osc = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      const gain = ctx.createGain();\\n\\n      osc.type = \'triangle\';\\n      osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(2400, ctx.currentTime);\\n      osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(1800, ctx.currentTime + 0.07);\\n\\n      gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.12, ctx.currentTime);\\n      gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, ctx.currentTime + 0.07);\\n\\n      osc.connect(gain);\\n      gain.connect(ctx.destination);\\n\\n      osc.start();\\n      osc.stop(ctx.currentTime + 0.08);\\n    } catch {}\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Iconic JARVIS startup sequence: two-tone harmonic chime\\n   */\\n  public playJarvisChime(): void {\\n    if (this.isMuted) return;\\n    const ctx = this.initContext();\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const now = ctx.currentTime;\\n      const notes = [587.33, 880, 1174.66]; // D5, A5, D6\\n\\n      notes.forEach((freq, idx) => {\\n        const osc = ctx.createOscillator();\\n        const gain = ctx.createGain();\\n\\n        osc.type = \'sine\';\\n        osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq, now + idx * 0.1);\\n\\n        gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0, now + idx * 0.1);\\n        gain.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(0.15, now + idx * 0.1 + 0.03);\\n        gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, now + idx * 0.1 + 0.45);\\n\\n        osc.connect(gain);\\n        gain.connect(ctx.destination);\\n\\n        osc.start(now + idx * 0.1);\\n        osc.stop(now + idx * 0.1 + 0.5);\\n      });\\n    } catch {}\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Protocol alert siren / warning pulse\\n   */\\n  public playProtocolAlert(): void {\\n    if (this.isMuted) return;\\n    const ctx = this.initContext();\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const now = ctx.currentTime;\\n      [0, 0.22, 0.44].forEach((delay) => {\\n        const osc = ctx.createOscillator();\\n        const gain = ctx.createGain();\\n\\n        osc.type = \'sawtooth\';\\n        osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(650, now + delay);\\n        osc.frequency.linearRampToValueAtTime(950, now + delay + 0.12);\\n\\n        gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.14, now + delay);\\n        gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.01, now + delay + 0.18);\\n\\n        osc.connect(gain);\\n        gain.connect(ctx.destination);\\n\\n        osc.start(now + delay);\\n        osc.stop(now + delay + 0.2);\\n      });\\n    } catch {}\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Arc Reactor power surge / charge-up sweep\\n   */\\n  public playReactorCharge(): void {\\n    if (this.isMuted) return;\\n    const ctx = this.initContext();\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const osc = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      const gain = ctx.createGain();\\n\\n      osc.type = \'sine\';\\n      osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(150, ctx.currentTime);\\n      osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(1200, ctx.currentTime + 0.6);\\n\\n      gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.02, ctx.currentTime);\\n      gain.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(0.18, ctx.currentTime + 0.4);\\n      gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, ctx.currentTime + 0.65);\\n\\n      osc.connect(gain);\\n      gain.connect(ctx.destination);\\n\\n      osc.start();\\n      osc.stop(ctx.currentTime + 0.7);\\n    } catch {}\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const sound = new SoundSynthesizer();\\n\",\"Description\":\"Synthesizer for JARVIS HUD sound effects (startup chime, click, scan blip, alerts, reactor charge)\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/soundEffects.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating soundEffects.ts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create Web Audio sound effects utility\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
