  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Intent**\n\nI am currently dissecting the user\'s request. It seems they want to make an existing element, perhaps a screen or concept, modifiable for their needs. I am focused on understanding the implications of \"make it here available\" and \"let me make changes.\" I\'m determining if this involves an editable copy, a shared interface, or something more complex.\n\n\n**Envisioning Interactive Simulation**\n\nI\'m now picturing a web-based scenario builder. The goal is to bring a mobile hands-free Jarvis simulation and scenario editor directly into a browser. Users can interact with a live simulator, run scenarios, and make changes to custom voice commands, steps, reasoning, confirmations, actions, and voices in real-time within the web app. It\'s becoming clearer.\n\n\n**Expanding Scenario Capabilities**\n\nI\'m expanding the scenario builder to incorporate new tools like WhatsApp/SMS sending, thermostat control, calendar events, music playback, and more. My focus is on integrating these into both hands-free and interactive modes. I\'m also ensuring seamless integration with the full JARVIS suite, providing a toggle between the scenario studio and the Stark HUD. I\'m prioritizing user-friendliness, allowing users to edit existing scenarios and add their own.\n\n\n**Integrating Scenario Features**\n\nI am now focusing on the implementation details. I want users to run scenarios as either automated walkthroughs or hands-free. I\'m reviewing existing project files, especially `src/App.tsx`, to integrate cleanly. I\'m exploring adding a switcher or dedicated tabs: `[ \360\237\223\261 Hands-Free Phone & Scenarios ]` and `[ \342\232\241 Stark HUD Command Center ]`. I\'m also visualizing the UI, a hands-free phone screen with status bar, scenario picker, agent state display (\"Idle,\" \"Listening,\" etc.), and scripted walkthroughs showcasing the code\'s execution flow.\n\n\n**Defining User Editing Focus**\n\nI now understand the user\'s need perfectly: they want an editable scenario experience. I\'m focusing on \"and let me make changes of it for me\"! My emphasis is on empowering users to modify, create custom scenarios, adjust voice interactions and confirmations, and instantly test their changes within the browser. I am thinking of a `HandsFreeStudio.tsx` component with an interactive phone frame and a clear flow visualization.\n\n\n**Designing Scenario Features**\n\nI am now visualizing the scenario selector. It will offer pre-built scenarios, such as messaging, phone calls, smart home interactions, and calendar entries. I am thinking of a built-in library, including a messaging scenario (\"Message Happy Hogan\"), phone calls (\"Call Pepper Potts\"), smart home control (\"Workshop Thermostat to 68\302\260F\"), and other options. I\'m focusing on user ability to edit, and create new scenarios, including fields for title, icon, trigger, voice input, Jarvis intent, and actions like sending messages or making calls.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1651345"
      name: "view_file"
