  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request\'s Scope**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. It seems they want voice-controlled access to all phone data, enabling simultaneous searches across multiple applications. The challenge lies in interpreting the \"everything\" aspect and its implications for privacy and system resources. I\'m focusing on defining the scope of \"everything\" and identifying potential bottlenecks.\n\n\n**Defining Core User Intent**\n\nI\'ve identified the core user intent as universal voice control of phone functions. This expands beyond just data access, encompassing system toggles and app interactions. I\'m focusing on creating an \"Interactive Phone Subsystem Access Center\" that allows granular permission control and simulated app control via voice, aiming for a system like a personal assistant. I\'m still working on \"looking for something in the ai\".\n\n\n**Developing Multi-AI Query**\n\nI\'m now designing a multi-AI simultaneous query system. My current focus is on a parallel execution engine (\"Omni-AI Dispatcher\") that can simultaneously execute queries across several top AI models (Gemini, Claude, GPT, Perplexity, DeepSeek, and Groq). I\'m visualizing live execution cards with real-time streaming results from each model. The goal is to compare outputs and synthesize the \"Best Combined Result,\" highlighting consensus, unique insights, and actionable answers.\n\n\n**Implementing the Parallel Engine**\n\nI\'m now concretely defining the architecture for the \"Omni-AI Dispatcher.\" This will use a `POST /api/multi-ai-search` endpoint in `server.ts` to manage the simultaneous queries to Gemini, Claude, GPT-4o, Perplexity, and DeepSeek. My goal is for this to provide simulated/grounded multi-model responses. This system will also provide a \"Stark Unified Consensus Verdict\", with built-in fallbacks. The response will include model details, consensus, and recommended action.\n\n\n**Visualizing The UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the user interface for the parallel AI query module. I envision a clean, futuristic UI displaying the live status of queries across all six engines with progress bars for each model. The \"Best Result\" master card will highlight the synthesized verdict and have a voice readout. I also plan a side-by-side comparison grid to showcase each model\'s strengths, response times, and results. This will be entirely voice-triggered for ease of use.\n\n\n**Expanding Phone Control Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the scope to full voice control of all phone functions. I\'m focusing on \"Interactive Phone Subsystem Access Center\" interactions, now encompassing phone calls, camera features with object recognition, photo searches, settings toggles (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, flashlight!), file access, calendar management, and GPS. I will be making voice commands like \"EDITH, what\'s my next meeting?\", and implementing the system fully.\n\n\n"
