tudio App\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta property=\\\\\\\"og:description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"\\n<truncated 172 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.html\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update index.html metadata and fonts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":19,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T15:59:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":3303,\"cache_read_tokens\":43709,\"output_tokens\":1250,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Utility Options**\\n\\nI\'m now investigating potential optional utilities like `canvas-confetti`, while noting the existing use of `motion` and `lucide-react`. I\'m also examining the `package.json` scripts to understand their role in the project setup.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Full-Stack Deployment**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on integrating full-stack functionality. I\'ve modified the `package.json` scripts to align with the full-stack design. I\'m updating \\\"dev\\\" to use `tsx server.ts`, adding a \\\"start\\\" script for produc\\n<truncated 540 bytes>\\nd to deliver a British aristocratic cadence, while providing concise, action-oriented answers.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Fallback Strategies**\\n\\nI\'m now devising fallback mechanisms for API failures. In case the Gemini API key is missing or a request fails, I\'ll gracefully activate a built-in J.A.R.V.I.S. responder. This will ensure uninterrupted service and an authentic Stark AI dialogue. I\'ve also incorporated fallback for the text-to-speech API. If it fails, the client seamlessly uses `SpeechSynthesis` instead.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Configure dev and start scripts for full-stack server.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"12\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update scripts to run tsx server.ts for dev and node server.ts for start\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    \\\\\\\"dev\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"tsx server.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"build\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite build\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"start\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"node server.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"preview\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite preview\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"clean\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rm -rf dist\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"lint\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"tsc --noEmit\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"7\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    \\\\\\\"dev\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"build\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite build\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"preview\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite preview\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"clean\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rm -rf dist server.js\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"lint\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"tsc --noEmit\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating package.json scripts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update package.json scripts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":21,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:00:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":3776,\"cache_read_tokens\":45200,\"output_tokens\":3726,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Server Logic**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `server.ts` file, ensuring it\'s built with modern ESM, robust typing, and integrating `@google/genai` with the specified User-Agent. I\'m focusing on solid error handling. Currently, I am also figuring out how to construct the Vite middleware.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Middleware Integration**\\n\\nI\'m now incorporating Express middleware to handle API endpoints. I have `/api/chat`, `/api/tts`, and a `/api/health` check ready to go. I\'m focusing on defining routes and in\\n<truncated 473 bytes>\\ng for initialization. I\'m now integrating the fallback logic for handling the \'/api/chat\' endpoint and setting up the system instruction.\\n\\n\\n**Assessing Tactical Directives**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating the user directives. Addressing you as ${userTitle}, I\'m processing your tactical instructions within the `protocol` state. The suit deployed is ${suit}. Telemetry is confirming the optimal response to the user\'s commands for the current context. I am ready to implement the given actions to optimize the response.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import express from \'express\';\\\\nimport dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\\\nimport path from \'path\';\\\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\\\\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \'@google/genai\';\\\\n\\\\ndotenv.config();\\\\n\\\\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\\\\nconst __d\\n<truncated 9346 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create server.ts Express backend with Gemini chat, TTS, fallback intelligence, and Vite middleware\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating server.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Express server entry point\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":23,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:00:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":3998,\"cache_read_tokens\":49134,\"output_tokens\":238,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing CSS Styling**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on `src/index.css`. My plan involves integrating custom futuristic Stark HUD elements: animations, neon borders, scanlines, and radial gradients. The file presently only imports Tailwind CSS. I\'m exploring how to expand this foundation.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View src/index.css\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":25,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:00:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2584,\"cache_read_tokens\":51032,\"output_tokens\":2995,\"thinking\":\"**Developing CSS for Project**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on developing `src/index.css` with Tailwind v4, anticipating custom HUD styling. I\'ve confirmed that `@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";` works as expected. Now, I\'m defining custom theme rules and utility classes to personalize the look. I have started by defining a root variable for --hud-cyan.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Styles, Fonts & Glows**\\n\\nI\'ve defined a suite of custom variables for HUD colors including cyan, blue, amber, and crimson, along with dimmed variants, in the r\\n<truncated 134 bytes>\\ncts with box-shadows and text-shadows, creating glow-cyan, amber, and crimson variations with different intensities.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Visual Effects**\\n\\nI\'ve crafted `glow-text` utility classes for amber and crimson text effects. I\'m focusing on a scanline effect using a linear gradient, and I\'m developing a tech grid background. I\'ve also defined spin and pulse animation keyframes for dynamic elements. Now, I\'m working to integrate these into the larger design, and I\'m testing the animations and effects.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n@layer base {\\\\n  :root {\\\\n    --hud-cyan: #00f0ff;\\\\n    --hud-cyan-dim: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);\\\\n    --hud-blue: #0284c7;\\\\n    --hud-amber: #f59e0b;\\\\n    --hud-crimson: #ef4444;\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  body {\\\\n    background-color: #020611;\\n<truncated 2994 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add Stark HUD styling, sci-fi animations, glowing utilities, and custom fonts\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Write HUD CSS styles\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":27,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:00:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":3249,\"cache_read_tokens\":53740,\"output_tokens\":2657,\"thinking\":\"**Planning Application Architecture**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on architecting the JARVIS application. I\'ve begun outlining the essential components and audio tools needed for an impressive interface. Specifically, I\'m considering using `src/utils/soundEffects.ts` with a real-time Web Audio API sound synthesizer, including functions like `playBeep(freq, type, duration)`. My aim is to define the ideal structure.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Audio Framework**\\n\\nI\'m now refining the audio framework. I\'ve got `playJarvisChime()`, the \\n<truncated 618 bytes>\\noice dictation, quick protocol buttons, and a real-time audio player. I\'m also planning to incorporate sound effects.\\n\\n\\n**Designing Armory & Power Modules**\\n\\nI\'m currently fleshing out the armory and power components. I\'m focusing on the `ArmoryModule`, implementing Stark armor schematics, telemetry, and deploy actions with HUD alerts. For the `PowerMatrixModule`, I\'m developing Arc Reactor power routing, distribution sliders, and emergency divert presets. Finally, I\'ll integrate a tactical radar module.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Web Audio API synthesizer for sci-fi JARVIS HUD sound effects.\\\\n * Synthesizes audio entirely in-browser without external asset dependencies.\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nclass SoundSynthesizer {\\\\n  private ctx: AudioContext | null = null;\\\\n  public isMuted: boolean =\\n<truncated 4631 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Synthesizer for JARVIS HUD sound effects (startup chime, click, scan blip, alerts, reactor charge)\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/soundEffects.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating soundEffects.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Web Audio sound effects utility\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":29,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:01:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":2912,\"cache_read_tokens\":57219,\"output_tokens\":1797,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Speech Recognition**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on defining the `speech.ts` utility. My current goal is creating a class or module to manage speech-to-text functionality. This involves handling recognition with `webkitSpeechRecognition` or `SpeechRecognition`, along with the necessary event handlers for results, errors, and end-of-speech. I\'ll need to track the microphone state as well.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Speech Recognition (STT) and Vocal Synthesis (TTS) module for J.A.R.V.I.S.\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nexport interface SpeechRecognitionHandlers {\\\\n  onStart?: () => void;\\\\n  onResult?: (transcript: string, isFinal: boolean) => void;\\\\n  onError?: (error: string) => \\n<truncated 5538 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Speech controller for voice recognition and text-to-speech with Gemini TTS and browser fallback\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/speech.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating speech.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Speech Recognition and Synthesis utility\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":31,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:01:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":4155,\"cache_read_tokens\":57971,\"output_tokens\":2856,\"thinking\":\"**Designing the Arc Reactor**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m diving into the `ArcReactor.tsx` component. The focus is on authentic Stark Industries design. I\'m visualizing a central, luminous core with a palladium or vibranium glow\342\200\224that\'s the key. I want it to be immediately recognizable as a technological marvel.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Zap, Flame, ShieldAlert, Cpu } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface ArcReactorProps {\\\\n  isSpeaking: boolean;\\\\n  isProcessing: boolean;\\\\n  isListening: boolean\\n<truncated 8051 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Interactive holographic Arc Reactor with spinning magnetic coils, reactive pulse rings, and telemetry\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ArcReactor.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ArcReactor.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create holographic Arc Reactor component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":33,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:01:53Z\",\"input_tokens\":3115,\"cache_read_tokens\":62049,\"output_tokens\":3038,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing HUD Header Components**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `src/components/HudHeader.tsx` file. My goal is to craft the visual layout and functionality. I\'m focusing on incorporating the Stark Industries branding, the J.A.R.V.I.S. Core version, and the real-time clock, which will display UTC, local time, and the elapsed time for the active mission. I\'m exploring the best approach to ensure each element is visually appealing and correctly formatted.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  VolumeX,\\\\n  Mic,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  Activity,\\\\n  Sliders,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Settings,\\\\n  HelpCircle,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\\\n<truncated 9438 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Stark HUD Header with mission timer, satellite uplink telemetry, audio controls, honorific selector, and protocol trigger\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create HUD Header component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":35,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:02:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":3303,\"cache_read_tokens\":65121,\"output_tokens\":3540,\"thinking\":\"**Designing the Command Center**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the design of `CommandCenter.tsx`. My current focus is integrating a real-time conversation stream with J.A.R.V.I.S. I plan to implement a dynamic typing effect for J.A.R.V.I.S.\'s responses to enhance the interactive experience within the conversation terminal.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Send,\\\\n  Mic,\\\\n  MicOff,\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  RefreshCw,\\\\n  Terminal,\\\\n  ShieldCheck,\\\\n  Zap,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Bot,\\\\n  User,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } fr\\n<truncated 10975 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Tactical Neural Terminal and CommandCenter with conversational stream, voice recognition input, quick protocols, and read-aloud buttons\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/CommandCenter.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating CommandCenter.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create CommandCenter terminal component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":37,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:02:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":3823,\"cache_read_tokens\":68335,\"output_tokens\":3719,\"thinking\":\"**Building Tactical Modules**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on constructing the tactical modules. Specifically, I\'ve started outlining the `ArmoryModule.tsx`. It\'ll feature a Stark Armor Database and Holographic schematics. I\'m planning to include the Mark VII, XLII, XLIV (Hulkbuster/Veronica), L (Nanotech), and LXXXV (Nano-Gauntlet).\\n\\n\\n**Developing Functional Modules**\\n\\nI\'ve been working on functional modules, and have made substantial headway. I\'m focusing on the `PowerMatrixModule.tsx` component, the Arc Reactor power management system, including real-time power routing across various systems. I\'m excited about the overclock toggle, allowing up to 135% output. I\'ve also incorporated preset tactics for enhanced operational efficiency.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Shield, Zap, Wind, Cpu, Crosshair, CheckCircle2, ChevronRight } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface ArmorSuit {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n  mark: string;\\\\n  d\\n<truncated 10816 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Stark Armory module with interactive armor platforms (Mark 85, Mark 50, Hulkbuster, Mark 42, Mark 7) and technical telemetry\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ArmoryModule.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ArmoryModule.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Stark Armory component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":39,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:03:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":4010,\"cache_read_tokens\":72150,\"output_tokens\":2633,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Power Matrix Module**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on defining the features for `src/components/PowerMatrixModule.tsx`. The key aspect I\'m considering is arc reactor power routing. I\'ve broken this down into three components: Repulsors (with a default of 30%), Flight Thrusters (25%), and the Unibeam Focal Lens (20%). I\'m thinking about the default power allocation for each of these components.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Zap, Gauge, Flame, AlertTriangle, ShieldCheck, BatteryCharging, Radio } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface PowerMatrixProps {\\\\n  powerLevel: number;\\\\n  onPow\\n<truncated 7830 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Arc Reactor Power Routing Matrix component with power throttle, combat presets, and subsystem channels\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/PowerMatrixModule.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating PowerMatrixModule.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Power Matrix module\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":41,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:03:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":2876,\"cache_read_tokens\":76129,\"output_tokens\":3471,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Radar Module Features**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on defining the features for `src/components/TacticalRadarModule.tsx`. It\'ll have a 360-degree rotating radar screen with a scanline sweep. The radar will display targets, specifically Veronica Orbital Platform, Stark Satellite Mesh (both friendly), and Sub. I\'m visualizing the dynamic movement and display capabilities.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Radar as RadarIcon, Compass, Radio, Wind, Thermometer, ShieldAlert, Navigation } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface RadarTarget {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  name: str\\n<truncated 10421 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Tactical Radar and Atmospheric telemetry module with interactive radar sweep and target inspector\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/TacticalRadarModule.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating TacticalRadarModule.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Tactical Radar component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":43,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:03:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":3747,\"cache_read_tokens\":78927,\"output_tokens\":3493,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Modal Component**\\n\\nI\'m working on the `ProtocolMatrixModal.tsx` component now. I\'ve begun to define its core features, focusing initially on the Stark Protocol Execution. I\'m considering two key protocols: the House Party Protocol, which deploys autonomous combat armor, and the Clean Slate Protocol, a security measure that detonates auxiliary armor units.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  X,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  Zap,\\\\n  Users,\\\\n  Compass,\\\\n  CheckCircle,\\\\n  Lock,\\\\n  Unlock,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface Protocol\\n<truncated 11577 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Stark Protocol Override Matrix modal with House Party, Clean Slate, Veronica, and security override controls\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ProtocolMatrixModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ProtocolMatrixModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Protocol Matrix modal component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":45,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:04:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":3766,\"cache_read_tokens\":82593,\"output_tokens\":4139,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing App.tsx**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the construction of `src/App.tsx`. My current focus is integrating the state management aspects. Specifically, I\'m working with the `userTitle`, which will be configurable, and I\'m also including the `suitModel`, set to \'Mark LXXXV\'. This should be an interesting component to bring together.\\n\\n\\n**Defining State and Handlers**\\n\\nI\'ve been defining the state variables needed within the app, specifically drawing data from the `ArmoryModule`. I am focusing on the properties, such as `powerLevel`, `currentProtocol`, and UI-related states like `activeTab`, `isSpeaking`, `voiceEnabled`, and so on. Simultaneously, I\'ve started building the `handleSendMessage` function, which will manage message sending and API interactions. It\'s designed to add user messages to the chat, manage the processing state, and send the necessary data to the `/api/chat` endpoint.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Terminal,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  Zap,\\\\n  Radar as RadarIcon,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Cpu,\\\\n  Layers,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { HudHeader } from \'./components/Hud\\n<truncated 12932 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Complete JARVIS main App component coordinating Arc Reactor, Command Center, Armory, Power Matrix, Tactical Radar, and Stark protocols\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Write App component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":47,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:04:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":4435,\"cache_read_tokens\":86379,\"output_tokens\":63,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet to check for build errors\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":49,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:04:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":2295,\"cache_read_tokens\":88664,\"output_tokens\":66,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running linter\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run applet linter\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":51,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:05:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":2318,\"cache_read_tokens\":88808,\"output_tokens\":76,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":53,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:05:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":2305,\"cache_read_tokens\":88976,\"output_tokens\":99,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/health\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking health endpoint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check API health\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":55,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:05:15Z\",\"input_tokens\":2361,\"cache_read_tokens\":89129,\"output_tokens\":85,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"3cb39ce0-0105-44f0-aba0-7ab0d9e76c02/task-54\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking task status\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check task status\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":58,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:05:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":2591,\"cache_read_tokens\":89330,\"output_tokens\":594,\"content\":\"Your app has been named **JARVIS** and initialized with a full-stack Stark Industries cybernetic interface:\\n\\n* **Authentic J.A.R.V.I.S. Neural Core**: Powered by Gemini (`gemini-3.8-flash`) with J.A.R.V.I.S.\'s calm, razor-sharp British wit, tactical analysis, and customizable forms of address (*Sir, Boss, Tony, Doctor, Commander*).\\n* **Vocal Synthesis & Hands-free Speech**: Voice dictation via Web Speech API and vocal playback via Gemini TTS with seamless browser fallback.\\n* **Interactive Holographic Arc Re\\n<truncated 398 bytes>\\npower routing across Repulsor Cannons, Supersonic Thrusters, Unibeam, Cockpit Life Support, and Sensor Grids with mission presets (*Max Firepower, Mach 7 Intercept, Stealth Recon*).\\n* **Tactical 360\302\260 Radar & Atmospheric Telemetry**: Real-time rotating radar sweep, orbital target tracking, and meteorological telemetry.\\n* **Stark Protocol Matrix**: Interactive execution system for the *House Party Protocol*, *Clean Slate Protocol* (with manual biometric override), *Veronica Orbital Drop*, and *Stealth Mode*.\",\"thinking\":\"**Verifying System Status**\\n\\nThe system check confirms the core is online with an attached API key, and a clean timestamp. It appears the development server is active. I see no initial problems. The system is ready.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":59,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:06:05Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nmake it here available and let me make changes of it for me\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-16T09:06:05-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-2kddokwqdskqllwzgox4ou-213045730586.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-2kddokwqdskqllwzgox4ou-213045730586.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: saiphotos1223@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"media\":[{\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"uri\":\"Voice Agent Preview.md\"}]}\n{\"step_index\":60,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:06:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":3097,\"cache_read_tokens\":89786,\"output_tokens\":1649,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing User Intent**\\n\\nI am currently dissecting the user\'s request. It seems they want to make an existing element, perhaps a screen or concept, modifiable for their needs. I am focused on understanding the implications of \\\"make it here available\\\" and \\\"let me make changes.\\\" I\'m determining if this involves an editable copy, a shared interface, or something more complex.\\n\\n\\n**Envisioning Interactive Simulation**\\n\\nI\'m now picturing a web-based scenario builder. The goal is to bring a mobile hands-free Jar\\n<truncated 1879 bytes>\\nselector. It will offer pre-built scenarios, such as messaging, phone calls, smart home interactions, and calendar entries. I am thinking of a built-in library, including a messaging scenario (\\\"Message Happy Hogan\\\"), phone calls (\\\"Call Pepper Potts\\\"), smart home control (\\\"Workshop Thermostat to 68\302\260F\\\"), and other options. I\'m focusing on user ability to edit, and create new scenarios, including fields for title, icon, trigger, voice input, Jarvis intent, and actions like sending messages or making calls.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"70\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx imports and state\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx state structure\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":62,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:06:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":2913,\"cache_read_tokens\":93356,\"output_tokens\":14423,\"thinking\":\"**Adding Hands-Free Mode**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on expanding the app\'s tab options in `App.tsx`. I plan to introduce a \'handsfree\' tab, which can accommodate either \'\360\237\223\261 Hands-free Mode & Scenarios\' or \'Hands-free Studio\'. I believe this feature will be a valuable addition.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Hands-Free Features**\\n\\nI\'ve been iterating on the \'hands-free\' functionality. It seems best to make \'Hands-free Studio\' a primary mode toggle in the top bar, alongside its tab presence. This allows quick access to the ex\\n<truncated 3148 bytes>\\nelds, voice prompts, Jarvis reasoning descriptions, tool selection with arguments, and customizable confirmation prompts with no-confirmation toggles. There is also an \\\"instant test\\\" button. I\'m also planning localStorage persistence and a \\\"reset to defaults\\\" option.\\n\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on the style and design. I\'m recreating a phone preview with a top bar, title, audio visualizer, agent state indicator, and interactive step player, including play/pause controls, step controls, and an autoplay toggle.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect, useRef } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Smartphone,\\\\n  Play,\\\\n  Pause,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  XCircle,\\\\n  Edit3,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Trash2,\\\\n  Save,\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  VolumeX,\\\\n  MessageSquare,\\\\n  Phone,\\\\n  Home,\\\\n  Music\\n<truncated 47880 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Hands-free mobile simulator and scenario studio with customizable user voice commands, agent reasoning, confirmation flows, and device execution\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create HandsFreeStudio component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":64,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:08:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":15238,\"cache_read_tokens\":96486,\"output_tokens\":243,\"thinking\":\"**Prioritizing Accessibility of Modes**\\n\\nI\'m currently updating `src/App.tsx` to prominently feature the new Hands-free Studio as both a main mode and a tab. The goal is to provide a clear and intuitive mode switcher at the top, allowing easy access to the requested interactive walkthrough and scenario editor via a mobile hands-free mode, and eventually also to some other new mode, likely a fast one.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"160\",\"StartLine\":\"120\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx tabs\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx tabs section\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":66,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:08:26Z\",\"input_tokens\":3270,\"cache_read_tokens\":109603,\"output_tokens\":88,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"240\",\"StartLine\":\"170\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx main tabs rendering\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx main tabs rendering\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":68,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:08:32Z\",\"input_tokens\":4017,\"cache_read_tokens\":110633,\"output_tokens\":86,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"317\",\"StartLine\":\"270\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx tab switches\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx remaining tabs\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":70,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:08:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":3030,\"cache_read_tokens\":112455,\"output_tokens\":911,\"thinking\":\"**Adding HandsFree Tab**\\n\\nI\'m currently modifying `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve imported `HandsFreeStudio` and `Smartphone` icons, as suggested. I\'m also adding `\'handsfree\'` to the `activeTab` type, allowing this new tab to be rendered. This involves adjusting the tab configuration to incorporate the new \'handsfree\' option.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add HandsFreeStudio import and update activeTab type\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"30\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import HandsFreeStudio and Smartphone, and set default activeTab to handsfree\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  Terminal,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  Zap,\\\\n  Radar as RadarIcon,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Cpu,\\\\n  Layers,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n  Smartphone,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { HudHeader } from \'./components/HudHeader\';\\\\nimport { ArcReactor } from \'\\n<truncated 930 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  Terminal,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  Zap,\\\\n  Radar as RadarIcon,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Cpu,\\\\n  Layers,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { HudHeader } from \'./components/HudHeader\';\\\\nimport { ArcReactor } from \'./components/Ar\\n<truncated 834 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx imports and state\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add HandsFreeStudio to App.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":72,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:08:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":3649,\"cache_read_tokens\":113342,\"output_tokens\":1331,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add Handsfree tab in navigation bar and render HandsFreeStudio content\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"225\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add Hands-free tab option and render HandsFreeStudio component when handsfree tab is active\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"        {/* Navigation Tabs */}\\\\n        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto pb-1 no-scrollbar border-b border-cyan-500/20\\\\\\\">\\\\n          {[\\\\n            { id: \'handsfree\', label: \'\360\237\223\261 Hands-Free Simulator & Studio\', icon: Smartphone \\n<truncated 1900 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"180\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"        {/* Navigation Tabs */}\\\\n        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto pb-1 no-scrollbar border-b border-cyan-500/20\\\\\\\">\\\\n          {[\\\\n            { id: \'command\', label: \'Tactical Command\', icon: Terminal },\\\\n            { id: \\n<truncated 1739 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating tab navigation and view in App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add Handsfree tab and content to App.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":74,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:08:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":4020,\"cache_read_tokens\":114755,\"output_tokens\":58,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet to check for build errors\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":76,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:09:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":2300,\"cache_read_tokens\":116615,\"output_tokens\":59,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running linter\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet code\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":78,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:09:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":2321,\"cache_read_tokens\":116754,\"output_tokens\":47,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":80,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:09:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":2285,\"cache_read_tokens\":116916,\"output_tokens\":76,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/health\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing health endpoint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Test API health\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":82,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:09:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":2384,\"cache_read_tokens\":117038,\"output_tokens\":852,\"content\":\"The **JARVIS Hands-Free Mobile Simulator & Scenario Studio** is now available in your app, complete with a scenario customizer so you can make and test changes directly:\\n\\n### \360\237\223\261 1. Interactive Hands-Free Phone Simulation\\n* **Exact Mobile Flow**: Modeled after the hands-free interface (`9:00  5G  \342\226\256\342\226\256\342\226\256`, `# Jarvis - Hands-free`, dynamic visualizer, and states: *Idle \342\206\222 Listening \342\206\222 Deciding \342\206\222 Confirming \342\206\222 Acting \342\206\222 Done*).\\n* **\\\"What talking to it feels like\\\"**: Watch the automated scripted walkt\\n<truncated 1299 bytes>\\nt Live Testing**: Click **\\\"Save & Test Run\\\"** to immediately watch your customized scenario play out in the phone simulator.\\n* **Persistent Storage**: All custom edits and new scenarios are saved to your browser so they remain intact across sessions, with a one-click **\\\"Defaults\\\"** button to restore original templates.\\n\\nYou can switch between the **\360\237\223\261 Hands-Free Simulator & Studio** and the **\342\232\241 Tactical Command HUD** (with the 3D Arc Reactor, Stark Armory, and Power Matrix) using the top navigation bar.\",\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Output**\\n\\nI\'ve confirmed a successful `curl` execution (code 0!). I\'m currently focused on the response data, specifically the \\\"Hands-free Mobile Phone Simulator.\\\" I\'m examining its features like the screen recreation (`9:00 5G \342\226\256\342\226\256\342\226\256`, `# Jarvis - Hands-free`) and the state indicators (`Idle`, `Listening`).\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":83,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:11:33Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nchange the voice to edith in the spderman look for it in the online and make sure i need that voice for my assistant\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-16T09:11:33-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-2kddokwqdskqllwzgox4ou-213045730586.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-2kddokwqdskqllwzgox4ou-213045730586.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: saiphotos1223@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":84,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:11:34Z\",\"input_tokens\":120572,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":664,\"thinking\":\"**Investigating E.D.I.T.H. Voice**\\n\\nI\'m currently searching online to confirm the specific E.D.I.T.H. voice from *Spider-Man: Far From Home*. I\'m focusing on the details and trying to verify its availability for use as an assistant voice.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing E.D.I.T.H.\'s Characteristics**\\n\\nI\'ve confirmed E.D.I.T.H.\'s full meaning and Dawn Michelle King as the voice actor. I\'m noting the AI\'s personality: calm, articulate, and professional. The mid-Atlantic American diction is crucial. Currently, I\'m examining \\\"gemini-api/SKILL.md\\\" to see if any prebuilt voices match these qualities, focusing on finding a comparable TTS voice.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"search_web\",\"args\":{\"query\":\"\\\"\\\\\\\"E.D.I.T.H.\\\\\\\" voice Spider-Man Far From Home Dawn Michelle King lines\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching E.D.I.T.H. voice details\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search E.D.I.T.H. voice details\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":86,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:11:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":2371,\"cache_read_tokens\":120631,\"output_tokens\":676,\"thinking\":\"**Defining E.D.I.T.H.\'s Persona**\\n\\nI\'m currently fleshing out E.D.I.T.H.\'s voice persona. Focusing on a female, calm, articulate delivery that\'s poised, soothing, and authoritative - a Stark tactical intelligence voice. I\'m aiming for something that is very different from J.A.R.V.I.S. and F.R.I.D.A.Y.\'s style. I\'m thinking I\'ll have Dawn Michelle King do the voice.\\n\\n\\n**Refining E.D.I.T.H.\'s Characteristics**\\n\\nI\'ve been further refining E.D.I.T.H.\'s digital identity. I\'ve updated the `/api/tts` to use \\\"Kore,\\\" a female voice, with a calm, articulate, and poised style. I\'ve also incorporated the \\\"Even Dead, I\'m The Hero\\\" acknowledgment in `/api/chat` as an E.D.I.T.H. protocol. I\'m choosing from assistant voices like Samantha, Victoria, and Karen, with a slightly raised pitch, in `speech.ts`. Finally, I\'ll be adding an explicit voice persona selector in the UI.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"160\",\"StartLine\":\"110\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing server.ts tts endpoint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View TTS endpoint in server.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":88,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:11:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":3770,\"cache_read_tokens\":121037,\"output_tokens\":83,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"220\",\"StartLine\":\"160\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing server.ts TTS logic\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View TTS logic in server.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":90,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:12:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":3255,\"cache_read_tokens\":122601,\"output_tokens\":511,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing AI Personality**\\n\\nI\'m currently focusing on how the `server.ts` code defines the AI\'s persona. Specifically, lines 181-194 detail the \'speechMetadata\', describing an aristocratic, calm, sophisticated British male AI with a composed cadence. This metadata is paired with the voice configuration, referencing \'Charon\'. I am trying to determine how these settings work together.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Voice Options**\\n\\nI\'ve been working on integrating a new voice option: E.D.I.T.H., as indicated in the request body of `/api/tts`, which would utilize the \'Kore\' Gemini voice, with the associated \'speechMetadata\' detailing a calm, articulate female persona.  This involves modifying `/api/chat` to include E.D.I.T.H. within the system instruction. This will ensure the AI adopts the correct persona.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/utils/speech.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing speech.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View speech controller implementation\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":92,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:12:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":3201,\"cache_read_tokens\":125890,\"output_tokens\":5770,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Voice Persona**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on improving `src/utils/speech.ts`. I\'m adding a `voicePersona` property, defaulting to \'EDITH\', to give me a voice option between \'EDITH\' and \'JARVIS\'. This `voicePersona` is now being passed in the `/api/tts` body. I plan to use it in `speakWithBrowserSynthesis` next.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Voice Options**\\n\\nI\'ve determined the top female voices available via `window.speechSynthesis.getVoices()` to use when `voicePersona` is \'EDITH\'. I\'ve specifically targeted voices\\n<truncated 657 bytes>\\nonses maintain the specified cool and collected demeanor, even during tactical scenarios.\\n\\n\\n**Updating the UI**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on UI integration. I\'m adding a direct voice persona switcher to the `HudHeader.tsx`, showcasing E.D.I.T.H. with a cyan/blue AR motif. In `HandsFreeStudio.tsx`, I\'ll integrate an E.D.I.T.H. voice test button and a specific \\\"Authorize Orbital Drone Strike\\\" scenario to the scenario list for added user immersion. These updates bring significant visual and interactive improvements.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update server.ts to support E.D.I.T.H. persona, Kore female voice, and Spider-Man Far From Home tactical system instructions\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"212\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update fallback responses, chat endpoint, and TTS endpoint to support E.D.I.T.H. voice and persona\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"// Built-in intelligent fallback responses if API key is not configured or fails\\\\nfunction getFallbackResponse(\\\\n  prompt: string,\\\\n  userTitle: string = \'Peter\',\\\\n  suit: string = \'Mark LXXXV\',\\\\n  voicePersona: \'EDITH\' | \'JARVIS\' = \'EDITH\'\\\\n): string {\\\\n\\n<truncated 9234 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"30\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"// Built-in intelligent fallback responses if API key is not configured or fails\\\\nfunction getFallbackJarvisResponse(prompt: string, userTitle: string = \'Sir\', suit: string = \'Mark LXXXV\'): string {\\\\n  const lower = prompt.toLowerCase();\\\\n\\\\n  if (lower.in\\n<truncated 7977 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating server.ts for EDITH voice and persona\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update server.ts for EDITH support\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":94,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:12:41Z\",\"input_tokens\":9795,\"cache_read_tokens\":129074,\"output_tokens\":3565,\"thinking\":\"**Adding Voice Persona Parameter**\\n\\nI\'ve just added a `voicePersona` property to the `speech.ts` file, defaulting to \'EDITH\'. I\'m now passing this property to the `/api/tts` fetch body to control the voice selection. I\'m focusing on the `speakWithBrowserSynthesis` function to select a female voice if the `voicePersona` is set to \'EDITH\'.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update speech.ts to support E.D.I.T.H. voice persona as default and configure browser speech synthesis fallback\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"210\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add voicePersona to SpeechController, pass to API, and configure female E.D.I.T.H. voice fallback\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"class SpeechController {\\\\n  private recognition: any = null;\\\\n  private currentAudio: HTMLAudioElement | null = null;\\\\n  private isSpeaking: boolean = false;\\\\n  public voiceEnabled: boolean = true;\\\\n  public voicePersona: \'EDITH\' | \'JARVIS\' = \'EDITH\';\\\\n  \\n<truncated 6249 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"12\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"class SpeechController {\\\\n  private recognition: any = null;\\\\n  private currentAudio: HTMLAudioElement | null = null;\\\\n  private isSpeaking: boolean = false;\\\\n  public voiceEnabled: boolean = true;\\\\n  private onSpeakingChangeCallbacks: Set<(speaking: bool\\n<truncated 5197 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/speech.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating speech controller for EDITH\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update speech.ts for EDITH voice\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":96,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:01Z\",\"input_tokens\":5011,\"cache_read_tokens\":138726,\"output_tokens\":183,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"60\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing HudHeader.tsx props\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View HudHeader props\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":98,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":3325,\"cache_read_tokens\":141532,\"output_tokens\":90,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"180\",\"StartLine\":\"120\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing HudHeader settings section\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View HudHeader settings section\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":100,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":3523,\"cache_read_tokens\":142645,\"output_tokens\":1463,\"thinking\":\"**Refining HudHeaderProps**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on expanding `HudHeaderProps`. I plan to introduce `voicePersona`, which will be either \'EDITH\' or \'JARVIS\', and an `onVoicePersonaChange` function. This should allow toggling the voice persona in the `HudHeader` component itself. I need to make sure the implementation handles display of the voice persona badge or toggle.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Voice Persona Switch**\\n\\nI\'ve got the voice persona toggle button working in the `HudHeader` now. Clicking the button cyc\\n<truncated 134 bytes>\\n I also made sure to include \\\"Peter\\\" in the titles list. I\'m also adding an E.D.I.T.H. scenario to `HandsFreeStudio.tsx`!\\n\\n\\n**Deploying Orbital Drone Functionality**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating the orbital drone deployment functionality, triggering via a simulated E.D.I.T.H. command. I\'m adding a \\\"Test E.D.I.T.H. Voice\\\" button to `HandsFreeStudio.tsx` to streamline testing. I am also working on connecting the voice command to the backend to get the expected E.D.I.T.H. response and feedback loop into the AR HUD.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add voicePersona prop, Glasses icon, and E.D.I.T.H. voice selector in HudHeader\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"38\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update HudHeaderProps to include voicePersona and onVoicePersonaChange, and import Glasses icon\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  VolumeX,\\\\n  Mic,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  Activity,\\\\n  Sliders,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Settings,\\\\n  HelpCircle,\\\\n  Glasses,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface HudHeaderProps {\\\\n  userTitle:\\n<truncated 574 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  VolumeX,\\\\n  Mic,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  Activity,\\\\n  Sliders,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Settings,\\\\n  HelpCircle,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface HudHeaderProps {\\\\n  userTitle: string;\\\\n  \\n<truncated 419 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating HudHeader.tsx props\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update HudHeader props for EDITH voice\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":102,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:24Z\",\"input_tokens\":4112,\"cache_read_tokens\":144215,\"output_tokens\":146,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"75\",\"StartLine\":\"50\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing titles array in HudHeader\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View titles array in HudHeader\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":104,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":3097,\"cache_read_tokens\":146131,\"output_tokens\":92,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"200\",\"StartLine\":\"140\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing right controls in HudHeader\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View right controls in HudHeader\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":106,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":3514,\"cache_read_tokens\":147015,\"output_tokens\":3248,\"thinking\":\"**Adjusting Titles & Persona**\\n\\nI\'m currently updating the `titles` array to include \'Peter\', \'Sir\', \'Boss\', \'Tony\', \'Doctor\', and \'Parker\'. I plan to place the Voice Persona selector right next to the honorific within `HudHeader.tsx`. I\'ll be editing `src/components/HudHeader.tsx` to incorporate these changes.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update titles to include Peter and Parker, and add Voice Persona selector button\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"165\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add Peter and Parker to titles, and add Voice Persona toggle button for E.D.I.T.H. vs J.A.R.V.I.S.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  const titles = [\'Peter\', \'Sir\', \'Boss\', \'Tony\', \'Doctor\', \'Parker\'];\\\\n\\\\n  return (\\\\n    <header className=\\\\\\\"relative z-30 w-full border-b border-cyan-500/20 bg-slate-950/80 backdrop-blur-md px-4 py-2.5\\\\\\\">\\\\n      <div className=\\\\\\\"max-w-7xl mx-auto flex f\\n<truncated 5927 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"61\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  const titles = [\'Sir\', \'Boss\', \'Tony\', \'Doctor\', \'Commander\'];\\\\n\\\\n  return (\\\\n    <header className=\\\\\\\"relative z-30 w-full border-b border-cyan-500/20 bg-slate-950/80 backdrop-blur-md px-4 py-2.5\\\\\\\">\\\\n      <div className=\\\\\\\"max-w-7xl mx-auto flex flex-co\\n<truncated 4045 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/HudHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating HudHeader for EDITH voice\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update HudHeader with EDITH controls\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":108,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":5181,\"cache_read_tokens\":150380,\"output_tokens\":283,\"thinking\":\"**Defining the Initial State**\\n\\nI\'ve just added the `voicePersona` state to `App.tsx`, defaulting it to \'EDITH\'. I\'ve also set the `userTitle` to \'Peter\'. My immediate next step is to integrate a welcome message from E.D.I.T.H., setting the tone for the application\'s interactive persona.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"85\",\"StartLine\":\"20\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx state\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx state\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":110,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:13:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":3630,\"cache_read_tokens\":153424,\"output_tokens\":1803,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Initial Parameters**\\n\\nI\'ve begun by establishing some key default states in `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve set up `voicePersona` to default to \'EDITH\' and `userTitle` to \'Peter\'. I\'ve also added the initial greeting message: \\\"Hello, Peter. I am E.D.I.T.H., Tony Stark\'s augmented-reality security, defense, and tactical intelligence system. Even Dead, I\'m The Hero.\\\"\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Set E.D.I.T.H. voice persona, Peter user title, and pass persona to backend in App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"115\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add voicePersona state, update initial welcome message for E.D.I.T.H., and pass voicePersona to /api/chat\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export default function App() {\\\\n  const [userTitle, setUserTitle] = useState(\'Peter\');\\\\n  const [voicePersona, setVoicePersona] = useState<\'EDITH\' | \'JARVIS\'>(\'EDITH\');\\\\n  const [suitModel, setSuitModel] = useState(\'Mark LXXXV\');\\\\n  const [powerLevel, se\\n<truncated 2610 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"26\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export default function App() {\\\\n  const [userTitle, setUserTitle] = useState(\'Sir\');\\\\n  const [suitModel, setSuitModel] = useState(\'Mark LXXXV\');\\\\n  const [powerLevel, setPowerLevel] = useState(100);\\\\n  const [currentProtocol, setCurrentProtocol] = useSt\\n<truncated 2374 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx state and API payload for EDITH\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update App.tsx for EDITH persona\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":112,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:14:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":2760,\"cache_read_tokens\":157029,\"output_tokens\":121,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"185\",\"StartLine\":\"150\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing HudHeader invocation in App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View HudHeader invocation in App.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":114,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:14:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":3053,\"cache_read_tokens\":157600,\"output_tokens\":777,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Pass voicePersona and onVoicePersonaChange props to HudHeader in App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"182\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add voicePersona and onVoicePersonaChange to HudHeader\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"      {/* HUD Header */}\\\\n      <HudHeader\\\\n        userTitle={userTitle}\\\\n        onUserTitleChange={(title) => {\\\\n          setUserTitle(title);\\\\n          const notify: ChatMessage = {\\\\n            id: `msg-${Date.now()}`,\\\\n            sender: \'jarvis\'\\n<truncated 1393 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"162\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"      {/* HUD Header */}\\\\n      <HudHeader\\\\n        userTitle={userTitle}\\\\n        onUserTitleChange={(title) => {\\\\n          setUserTitle(title);\\\\n          const notify: ChatMessage = {\\\\n            id: `msg-${Date.now()}`,\\\\n            sender: \'jarvis\'\\n<truncated 565 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Passing voicePersona props in App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Pass voicePersona props in App.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":116,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:14:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":3458,\"cache_read_tokens\":158449,\"output_tokens\":603,\"thinking\":\"**Adding E.D.I.T.H. Test**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating an \\\"E.D.I.T.H. Voice Test\\\" button into the HandsFreeStudio. This will reside either on the phone frame or the top bar, allowing for direct triggering of a voice test. Pressing the button will initiate `speech.speakText(\\\"Hello, Peter. I am E.D.I.T.H.,\\\")` so the user can easily test the voice response.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing E.D.I.T.H. Scenario**\\n\\nI\'ve just added the \\\"E.D.I.T.H. Drone Target Lock\\\" scenario, inspired by Spider-Man: Far From Home, as a default option. It\'s under \\\"Stark Defense.\\\" The scenario includes the voice command, agent response, tool invocation (deploying orbital drones), and a confirmation prompt. The tool deploys orbital drones with a non-lethal EMP. It\'s pretty cool; even dead, I\'m the hero, right?\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"85\",\"StartLine\":\"30\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing DEFAULT_SCENARIOS in HandsFreeStudio\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DEFAULT_SCENARIOS in HandsFreeStudio\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":118,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:14:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":3771,\"cache_read_tokens\":159908,\"output_tokens\":108,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"440\",\"StartLine\":\"380\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing phone app header in HandsFreeStudio\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View phone app header in HandsFreeStudio\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":120,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:14:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":3886,\"cache_read_tokens\":161455,\"output_tokens\":1712,\"thinking\":\"**Updating the Scenario Listing**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on updating the scenario listing within `HandsFreeStudio.tsx`. I\'ve added the import for `Glasses` from `lucide-react`, and I am now inserting the Spider-Man E.D.I.T.H. scenario as the featured option at index 0 in `DEFAULT_SCENARIOS`.\\n\\n\\n**Adding New Spider-Man Scenario**\\n\\nI\'ve crafted a new Spider-Man tactical scenario, \\\"T.H. Tactical Drone Lock.\\\" I\'ve populated its details, including category, description, icon name, and the step with user speech, agent thought, tool name, tool arguments, confirmation prompt, action feedback, and notification data. The scenario focuses on an orbital drone lock, leveraging E.D.I.T.H.\'s capabilities, for use with the lucide-react library.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add Glasses import and E.D.I.T.H. scenario to DEFAULT_SCENARIOS in HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"70\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import Glasses and add E.D.I.T.H. tactical drone lock scenario to DEFAULT_SCENARIOS\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  Layers,\\\\n  ArrowRight,\\\\n  Glasses,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\nimport { speech } from \'../utils/speech\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface ScenarioStep {\\\\n  userSpeech: string;\\\\n  agentThought: string;\\\\n  toolName: string;\\n<truncated 1855 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"20\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  Layers,\\\\n  ArrowRight,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/soundEffects\';\\\\nimport { speech } from \'../utils/speech\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface ScenarioStep {\\\\n  userSpeech: string;\\\\n  agentThought: string;\\\\n  toolName: string;\\\\n  toolArgs\\n<truncated 636 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding EDITH scenario in HandsFreeStudio\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add EDITH scenario to HandsFreeStudio\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":122,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:14:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":2616,\"cache_read_tokens\":165404,\"output_tokens\":146,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"470\",\"StartLine\":\"415\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing action bar and phone header in HandsFreeStudio\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View action bar and phone header in HandsFreeStudio\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":124,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-16T16:14:46Z\",\"input_tokens\":3729,\"cache_read_tokens\":165803,\"output_tokens\":2202,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add Test E.D.I.T.H. Voice button and update phone title in HandsFreeStudio.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"465\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add Test E.D.I.T.H. Voice button and display # E.D.I.T.H. on phone header\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap\\\\\\\">\\\\n          <button\\\\n            onClick={() => {\\\\n              sound.playScanBlip();\\\\n              speech.voicePersona = \'EDITH\';\\\\n              speech.speakText(\\\\n                \\\\\\\"Hello, Pe\\n<truncated 3490 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"416\",\"TargetContent\