  planner_response {
    response: "The selected badge next to the assistant title has been removed.\n\n### Mobile Installation & Backend Deployment Guide\n\n#### 1. How to Install on Your Mobile Device\n* **Android (Chrome / Edge / Samsung Internet)**:\n  1. Open your shared app URL in **Google Chrome** on your phone.\n  2. Tap the **\"Install App\"** button at the top of the screen (or tap the browser menu `\342\213\256` and select **\"Add to Home Screen\"** / **\"Install app\"**).\n  3. The app will install as a standalone mobile app with its own icon, full-screen display, and microphone voice capabilities.\n* **iPhone / iPad (iOS Safari)**:\n  1. Open the app link in **Safari**.\n  2. Tap the **Share** button (the square with an arrow pointing up at the bottom).\n  3. Scroll down and select **\"Add to Home Screen\"**, then tap **Add**.\n  4. Launch the app directly from your home screen for the full-screen hands-free experience.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. How to Deploy with the Backend\nThe application runs as a unified full-stack Node.js + Express backend that serves the API and pre-compiled client assets:\n\n1. **Build the production assets**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   ```\n2. **Start the production server**:\n   ```bash\n   npm start\n   ```\n   *(Executes `node server.ts` on port 3000)*.\n\n3. **Cloud Deployment (Cloud Run, Render, Railway, VPS, or Docker)**:\n   * **Environment Variables**:\n     * `GEMINI_API_KEY`: Your Gemini API key for real-time neural responses and vocal synthesis.\n     * `PORT`: `3000` (or injected by your cloud host).\n     * `NODE_ENV`: `production`.\n   * **Build Command**: `npm run build`\n   * **Start Command**: `npm start`\n   * Both frontend and backend API endpoints (`/api/chat`, `/api/tts`, `/api/multiai`, `/api/phone/action`, `/api/health`) are served simultaneously on the same host with zero CORS friction."
    thinking: "**Verifying System Status**\n\nOkay, I\'ve just checked the health endpoint and confirmed the system status. It\'s online! The output shows the core version, voice, API key presence, and timestamp, all as expected. This helps ensure the system is operational. It seems that the response is what we are expecting from this endpoint, but we should continue checking the response regularly.\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Access**\n\nI\'ve integrated the E.D.I.T.H. voice persona, complete with a J.A.R.V.I.S-like interface. Voice command access is now implemented, and I\'ve established access control with voice authentication to secure the application. Unauthorized users will be denied access. The system is designed to fulfill every task requested with human-like behavior, including simultaneous searches across multiple AI platforms.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The selected badge next to the assistant title has been removed.\n\n### Mobile Installation & Backend Deployment Guide\n\n#### 1. How to Install on Your Mobile Device\n* **Android (Chrome / Edge / Samsung Internet)**:\n  1. Open your shared app URL in **Google Chrome** on your phone.\n  2. Tap the **\"Install App\"** button at the top of the screen (or tap the browser menu `\342\213\256` and select **\"Add to Home Screen\"** / **\"Install app\"**).\n  3. The app will install as a standalone mobile app with its own icon, full-screen display, and microphone voice capabilities.\n* **iPhone / iPad (iOS Safari)**:\n  1. Open the app link in **Safari**.\n  2. Tap the **Share** button (the square with an arrow pointing up at the bottom).\n  3. Scroll down and select **\"Add to Home Screen\"**, then tap **Add**.\n  4. Launch the app directly from your home screen for the full-screen hands-free experience.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. How to Deploy with the Backend\nThe application runs as a unified full-stack Node.js + Express backend that serves the API and pre-compiled client assets:\n\n1. **Build the production assets**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   ```\n2. **Start the production server**:\n   ```bash\n   npm start\n   ```\n   *(Executes `node server.ts` on port 3000)*.\n\n3. **Cloud Deployment (Cloud Run, Render, Railway, VPS, or Docker)**:\n   * **Environment Variables**:\n     * `GEMINI_API_KEY`: Your Gemini API key for real-time neural responses and vocal synthesis.\n     * `PORT`: `3000` (or injected by your cloud host).\n     * `NODE_ENV`: `production`.\n   * **Build Command**: `npm run build`\n   * **Start Command**: `npm start`\n   * Both frontend and backend API endpoints (`/api/chat`, `/api/tts`, `/api/multiai`, `/api/phone/action`, `/api/health`) are served simultaneously on the same host with zero CORS friction."
