  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Device Compatibility**\n\nI\'m focused on ensuring complete device compatibility. I\'m deep-diving into responsive design principles and determining the optimal breakpoints for mobile phones (360-430px), tablets (768-1024px), and desktops. I am currently considering implementing a fluid grid, and flexible images. I\'ll need to define clear strategies for content adaptation.\n\n\n**Expanding Device Considerations**\n\nI\'m now expanding my device compatibility focus to include laptops and ultra-wide screens (1440px - 2560px). I must consider touch-friendly tap targets, flexible font sizing, fluid layouts, and proper overflow handling. I\'m also adding mobile safe-area padding for notches and home bars.\n\n\n**Defining Access Protocols**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the granular access protocols. I\'m focusing on defining device permissions like microphone, camera, notifications, location, and storage. I am now working on security audit logs, including timestamps, facial scans, voice verifications, and intrusion attempts, and the system core configuration, and API choices (model selection, override systems)\n\n\n**Implementing Biometric Recognition**\n\nI\'m now implementing automatic background biometric scanning, ensuring seamless user recognition. I\'m focusing on a hidden canvas for video frame capture and `/api/biometrics/facial-scan` for backend processing. I\'m considering scenarios where camera permissions aren\'t granted, and have implemented multi-factor biometric fallback for secure and unobtrusive authentication.\n\n\n**Refining Biometric Verification**\n\nI\'m now refining the biometric verification process based on specific user requests. There will be no visible webcam preview; facial recognition occurs entirely in the background via the `/api/biometrics/facial-scan` endpoint. I\'m focusing on a subtle HUD indicator like \"BIOMETRIC: OPTICAL RETINAL SCAN IN PROGRESS [BACKGROUND]\" to show status, while implementing security lock protocol if an unknown face or unauthenticated voice is detected. I am also checking the existing codebase files: `src/App.tsx` and `src/components/HudHeader.tsx`.\n\n\n"
