  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the API endpoints for `server.ts`. The first, `/api/biometrics/facial-scan`, will accept optical frame data and client telemetry. I\'m considering both base64 image data and a visual feature matrix for the frame payload, alongside relevant client-side info like user agent and session ID.\n\n\n**Analyzing Biometric Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the facial recognition processor logic. My current focus is how the system handles image data. I\'ve designed it to leverage Gemini for multimodal evaluation, should a base64 image be provided. Otherwise, it uses the biometric pattern recognition engine. The system then attempts to match against the registered personnel. The response includes a match result with identity, confidence, and access details. Unauthorized faces trigger a different return.\n\n\n**Expanding API Endpoint Definitions**\n\nI\'m now expanding the API endpoints, specifically `/api/biometrics/facial-scan`. I\'m focusing on security and access control, integrating audit events for failed matches. I am now creating `/api/admin/system-status`, `/api/admin/audit-logs`, `/api/admin/users`, and `/api/admin/lockdown`. These will handle real-time biometric events, user management, and system lockdown functionalities, respectively. The `/api/biometrics/facial-scan` now includes an audit event log, as well.\n\nI am assessing client-side requirements for device compatibility. My focus is on ensuring UI layouts work for small mobile screens. I\'m focusing on various components, including `src/App.tsx`, `HudHeader.tsx`, `HandsFreeStudio.tsx`, and others. The initial focus is making the headers on small screens adaptable.\n\n\n**Refining UI Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m now implementing responsive UI layouts across device sizes. For smaller screens, I\'m working on flexible navigation, considering horizontal scrolling or compact tabs. I\'m focusing on font and padding scaling, ensuring components don\'t overflow, using responsive styling. I\'m also planning a bottom navigation bar or a floating action dock for quick access on mobile. I\'m adapting to tablets and desktops with 2-column grids and full HUD layouts with side-by-side telemetry, respectively. I\'m also adding viewport meta tags.\n\n\n**Designing UI Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI animation and visual feedback. I\'m exploring an arc reactor spin and reactive pulse for loading states. I\'m also planning interactive button micro-interactions, like magnetic glows and sound effects. I am also working on a security biometric scan overlay with an animated laser reticle and facial mesh overlay during background verification!\n\nI am now focusing on the account and admin settings aspect of the UI, creating a dedicated component, `src/components/AdminAccountSettings.tsx`. This includes profile & account overviews, voice protocol toggles, and device connections.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Settings**\n\nI\'ve just added `AdminAccountSettings.tsx`, focusing on profile overviews, voice protocol toggles, and device connections. I\'m now integrating this component into the navigation. The biometric sensitivity threshold slider is also being implemented, along with a silent background recognition toggle, and voiceprint authentication. I\'m planning to introduce RBAC with Director, Avenger, and Guest roles with granular permission toggles, like Orbital Drone Strike Authorization. Finally, I\'m designing a live security audit with biometric verifications and the emergency protocols.\n\n\n**Implementing Silent Biometrics**\n\nI\'m now building `src/utils/silentBiometrics.ts` for background facial recognition. This manager runs silently, without any on-screen prompts or previews. The system will initialize a headless `<video>` and `<canvas>` to grab optical data. I\'m prioritizing browser permission checks to ensure the camera can be accessed, then sending the frames to the `/api/biometrics/facial-scan` endpoint.\n\n\n**Integrating Silent Biometrics**\n\nI\'m now integrating multi-factor ambient biometric recognition, even without user gestures. The system leverages device optical profiles, credentials, a neural fingerprint, and audio analysis to match identities in the background. The backend returns verified identities and a discreet HUD indicator with smooth neon pulses. Unauthorized attempts trigger alerts and tactical subsystem lock-downs.\n\n\n"
