  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying PWA Prerequisites**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the foundational aspects needed for Progressive Web App (PWA) installation. The critical link is `beforeinstallprompt`, which is triggered by browsers like Chrome on Android. Per PWA standards, this requires both a valid Web App Manifest (like `manifest.webmanifest` or `manifest.json`) and a registered Service Worker. I will need to check if these prerequisites are met.\n\n\n**Confirming PWA Manifest**\n\nI\'ve got the manifest file (`public/manifest.webmanifest`) locked down, with critical PWA settings like `display: standalone` and icon configurations. I\'ve also implemented the minimal Service Worker (`public/sw.js`). My service worker skips waiting and claims clients on activation. The next step is to test its effectiveness for caching.\n\n\n"
